  "label": "The shocked woman is mapped as the reaction to the false biblical claim.",
  "description": "The visual entity 'woman_expressing_shock' is mapped onto the textual entity 'top_text' to represent the exaggerated shock or disbelief that the meme intends to convey in response to the false claim that 'Jesus command gays should be out to death?'. The woman's expression and gesture are used to visually amplify the perceived 'shock value' of the false claim, making the misinformation more emotionally compelling and virulent. This mapping is central to the meme's intent to provoke outrage and reinforce anti-LGBTQ+ religious rhetoric.",
